Subject: [PATCH] fix(display): probe the brightness clamp in a diagnostic image

Stacked on 0001, never alone: without it both fields of the request line read
2047 and the probe prints the defect itself instead of a difference. It exists
only to make 0001's C3 criterion reachable - the clamp in
K60BacklightCodec.h:62-67 only separates the two fields for an out-of-range
request, and a slider never sends one (2026-11-21, Lead).

Build-time switch, not a boot argument. k60_backlight_probe=1 was 21 bytes and
the 27 command line has 4 bytes left after O1, so the argument was withdrawn
before it ever reached a registry: BOOT-ARGS.md, BOOT-ARGS-PENDING.toml and the
ALLOWED_ADDITIONS set in scripts/check-image-args.py never contained it (grep
count 0 in each). The name is gone; K60_BACKLIGHT_PROBE replaces it and defaults
to 0 in the source, so every ordinary build compiles the block out.

Two images, same inputs, one switch:
  release     - no -D, block absent, strings prove it (see below);
  diagnostic  - -DK60_BACKLIGHT_PROBE=1, one line
                  K60 BACKLIGHT: brightness level 4095 -> level 2047 dbv 0xfff
                and the panel jumps to full brightness once at bring-up.

The absence is an assertion, not a promise: with the switch off the marker
string "K60 BACKLIGHT: probe request not built" must not appear in the built
kernel. docs/research/display/check-probe-absent.py reads a kernel.macho and
fails if it does; run it on both images and record the sha256s named in
docs/research/display/PROBE-BUILD-SWITCH.md.

Criteria: docs/research/display/BACKLIGHT-LOG-CRITERIA.md section 8.
Applies to the 27 ladder branch only.
---
--- a/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
+++ b/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
@@ -69,6 +69,17 @@ extern "C" {volatile int32_t native_backlight_stats[16];}
  * (0 no, 1 yes), [5] backlight-control published (0 no, 1 yes). */
 extern "C" {volatile int32_t native_backlight_request[6];}
 
+/* The clamp probe is a build-time switch, not a boot argument. A 21 byte
+ * argument does not fit beside the 27 line (4 bytes left after O1) and a key
+ * nothing reads is worse than no key, so release images compile this to 0 and
+ * the whole block disappears; only a dedicated diagnostic image passes
+ * -DK60_BACKLIGHT_PROBE=1. The absence is provable: with the switch off the
+ * marker string below does not exist in the built kernel
+ * (docs/research/display/PROBE-BUILD-SWITCH.md). */
+#ifndef K60_BACKLIGHT_PROBE
+#define K60_BACKLIGHT_PROBE 0
+#endif
+
 namespace {
 /* The newest request, goal << 16 | milliseconds, bit 63 set while the work loop
  * has not taken it yet. */
@@ -379,6 +390,33 @@ void K60Backlight::publishFirst(void)
           (int)native_backlight_request[0], (int)native_backlight_request[1],
           (int)native_backlight_request[4], (int)native_backlight_request[5],
           control ? "" : " (no AppleARMBacklight conformance)");
+
+#if K60_BACKLIGHT_PROBE
+    /* Stacked on 0001, never alone: without it both fields of the request line
+     * read 2047 and this prints the defect itself instead of a difference.
+     *
+     * Ask ourselves once, after the published line so that line keeps its
+     * documented req=0,0 invariant, for level 4095 - the top of the panel's own
+     * 12 bit DBV domain (kMaxDbv 0xfff), which is what a caller passes if it
+     * mistakes DBV units for levels. clampLevel() then lands it on 2047, so the
+     * expected line is
+     *
+     *   K60 BACKLIGHT: brightness level 4095 -> level 2047 dbv 0xfff
+     *
+     * Off in every release image: this block is not compiled at all unless the
+     * build passes -DK60_BACKLIGHT_PROBE=1. Side effect of a diagnostic image
+     * is one visible jump to full brightness at bring-up. */
+    OSDictionary *probe = OSDictionary::withCapacity(1);
+    OSNumber *probeLevel = OSNumber::withNumber(4095ULL, 32);
+    if (probe && probeLevel) {
+        probe->setObject("brightness", probeLevel);
+        setProperties(probe);
+    } else {
+        IOLog("K60 BACKLIGHT: probe request not built\n");
+    }
+    if (probeLevel) probeLevel->release();
+    if (probe) probe->release();
+#endif
 }
 
 IOReturn K60Backlight::setProperties(OSObject *properties)
